<h1>Current AirPods Lineup</h1>
<p>
  Every current AirPods model — AirPods 5, AirPods Pro 3, AirPods 4, AirPods 4 with ANC, and AirPods Max 2 — uses the H2 chip, which powers Adaptive Audio, Personalised Spatial Audio, Conversation Awareness, and low-latency Bluetooth processing. AirPods 5 stays on the H2 as well: its claimed 1.5x improvement in Active Noise Cancellation comes from a new acoustic architecture and driver, not new silicon. The only AirPods still on the older H1 are discontinued models.
</p>

